2015-08-31 15:30 GMT+03:00 Pierre Abbat <phma@bezitopo.org>:

> One of the questions added yesterday has the answer "seca'o". As far as I'm
> aware, this is ungrammatical; members of BAI may be converted with SE,
> which
> is equivalent to converting the corresponding brivla, but tense markers
> cannot.
>

This has already been discussed in IRC. Possible solutions:
1. ca su'o pagbu be ko'a
2. {ca lo nu ca'o broda} (i.e. invert the order or clauses that you need)
or {i ca bo ca'o broda}


> Related question: what is the Lojban for "tense" in the grammar sense,
> including spatial tenses?
>

Depends on which selmaho you want to include into your definition. Are TAhE
tenses, is "Present Continuous" a tense or not? Is {PA roi} a tense? Is
{fi'o fadni} a tense?



